NNOOTTEESS
       uuttmmppdduummpp can be useful in cases of corrupted utmp or wtmp entries. It
       can dump out utmp/wtmp to an ASCII file, which can then be edited to
       remove bogus entries, and reintegrated using:

          uuttmmppdduummpp --rr << aasscciiii__ffiillee >> wwttmmpp

       But be warned, uuttmmppdduummpp was written for debugging purposes only.

   FFiillee ffoorrmmaattss
       Only the binary version of the uuttmmpp(5) is standardised. Textual dumps
       may become incompatible in future.

       The version 2.28 was the last one that printed text output using
       ccttiimmee(3) timestamp format. Newer dumps use millisecond precision
       ISO-8601 timestamp format in UTC-0 timezone. Conversion from former
       timestamp format can be made to binary, although attempt to do so can
       lead the timestamps to drift amount of timezone offset.

BBUUGGSS
       You may nnoott use the --rr option, as the format for the utmp/wtmp files
       strongly depends on the input format. This tool was nnoott written for
       normal use, but for debugging only.

